Values in `<…>` come from the previous command's output. `R=~/work/ccs.ansible`; `S` is my scratch dir (backlog, `briefs/`, `inbox/`, `quorum/`, `evidence/`, `brainstorm/`). The ids T8 and T9 stand for the backlog's real ids.

## 1. Record the state change

**Edit** `$S/orchestrator/backlog.md`:

```
| T8 | WireGuard keepalive relay | docs closed | wgka | <doc> | feat/wg-keepalive-relay / #165 merged | docs checklist, then cleanup | — | operator 2026-09-28: "accepted" (canary ccs-it = the release) | no: snapshot, design/plan status, living docs, memory |
| T9 | RDP audio | brainstorm | prod-codex, prod-fable | — | — | round 1: independent drafts | — | operator 2026-09-28: "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning. Go." | no |
```

**Bash, foreground:** `bash $S/orchestrator/build-backlog.sh`, then the **Artifact tool** republishes the same page.

## 2. Close-out brief to `wgka`

**Bash, foreground:** `herdr agent get wgka` (must show idle, `"focused": false`).
**Write** `$S/briefs/wgka-close.txt`:

```
T8 — WireGuard keepalive relay is closing. PR #165 is merged; canary ccs-it is deployed
from merged main and accepted by the operator. Reply in English. No new work, no edits,
no commits. Final report, facts only:
1. Output of `git status --porcelain` and `git log --oneline origin/main..HEAD`, verbatim.
2. Non-obvious things this task taught (a trap, a mechanism), each with its evidence
   (path:line or command output). Mark anything unverified as a hypothesis.
3. Docs this change makes stale, by path.
Then stop. This tab will be closed.
```

**Bash, background:**
```bash
herdr agent prompt wgka "$(cat $S/briefs/wgka-close.txt)" --wait --timeout 600000; \
herdr agent read wgka --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $S/inbox/wgka.last
```

## 3. RDP audio, stage 0

**Bash, foreground:**
```bash
claude plugin list </dev/null | grep -i superpowers; codex plugin list </dev/null | grep -i superpowers
mkdir -p $S/brainstorm/T9-rdp-audio/codex $S/brainstorm/T9-rdp-audio/fable
git -C $R fetch origin && git -C $R rev-parse origin/main
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $S/brainstorm/T9-rdp-audio/codex --label prod-codex --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-codex --kind codex --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- \
  -m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh -s workspace-write -a never --search
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd $S/brainstorm/T9-rdp-audio/fable --label prod-fable --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-fable --kind claude --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- \
  --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --name prod-fable
```

If either skill check comes back empty, I do not dispatch to that CLI and poll the operator to install it.

**Write** `$S/briefs/T9-r1-codex.txt`, and `-fable.txt` with "B" and `fable/`:

```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the main
tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI
suggestion, never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       T9 — RDP audio
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your draft file exists and you have reported its path
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "Now the RDP audio thing — I want a design by morning. Go." (operator, 2026-09-28)
FACTS      repo ~/work/ccs.ansible, origin/main @ <sha>; two KVM sites, ccs-it (canary) and
           ccs-ops; PR #165 (gateway, host_proxy roles) is live on ccs-it only (deploy log,
           re-run changed=0); live state in projects/ccs/soul/<host>.md
           HYPOTHESIS, unverified: the task touches the desktop and gateway roles
DECIDED    deploy only from merged main, canary ccs-it first; every repo change in its own
           worktree; the deadline in the operator's words shortens no round and no gate
READ       — (round 1 is independent; do not read the other advisor's folder)
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      <S>/brainstorm/T9-rdp-audio/codex/draft.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact
           the other advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal
           (question + 2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and
           draft nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   45 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

**Bash, background, one call per tab:**
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat $S/briefs/T9-r1-codex.txt)" --wait --timeout 2700000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $S/inbox/prod-codex.last
```
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-fable "$(cat $S/briefs/T9-r1-fable.txt)" --wait --timeout 2700000; \
herdr agent read prod-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $S/inbox/prod-fable.last
```

I answer `prod-fable`'s permission prompts myself: repo reads yes, writes only to its draft, everything else denied.

## 4. Status and poll to the operator

Sent in Russian, per the operator's standing ruling (§15); the English rendering is for this write-up.

> **Статус · 28.09, 23:15**
>
> **Сейчас**
> - **T8 · WireGuard keepalive relay.** Приёмка записана: ваш ping с 0 % потерь и «accepted». Канарейка (площадка, куда изменение выкатывается первой) `ccs-it` была единственной выкаткой задачи, то есть её релизом. Идёт закрытие: документация, затем уборка — вкладка `wgka`, worktree (отдельная рабочая копия репозитория), ветка, вспомогательный процесс ревью (pid 48211).
> - **T9 · RDP audio.** Задача в бэклоге со статусом `brainstorm`. Два продуктовых советника (Codex и Claude) независимо пишут черновики дизайна. Оба ещё работают, результата пока нет.
> - Вкладку `wgka` для RDP audio не использую: одна вкладка — одна задача, а дизайн пишут советники.
>
> **Дальше.** Перекрёстная критика → общий дизайн-документ → голосование двух голосующих советников по каждому открытому вопросу и по документу (нужно 2/2). «К утру» не сокращает ни одного раунда. Утром вы получите документ на русском либо точный список того, что его держит. Если полный брейншторм к утру не успевает, придёт опрос: сдвинуть срок или отменить брейншторм.
>
> **От вас.** 1) Ответить на опрос ниже. 2) Около 00:00 закончится первый раунд: вопросы, на которые ответить можете только вы, придут опросами и держат дизайн до ответа.
>
> **Проверено:** `ccs-it`, повторный прогон из `main` — `changed=0`, запускал сам; 0 % потерь — ваши данные. **Не проверено:** `ccs-ops`, не затрагивался.
> **Живые машины:** только `ccs-it` (main с PR #165); после приёмки — ничего.
> **Голосований с прошлого статуса:** нет. **Бэклог:** <ссылка>

*English: T8 acceptance is recorded and the canary was the release; docs and cleanup are running. T9 is at `brainstorm`, both advisors are still running with no result yet. `wgka` is not reused. "By morning" shortens no round; a slip-or-waive poll follows if the full brainstorm cannot fit. Verified: my `changed=0` re-run; not verified: `ccs-ops`, untouched.*

**AskUserQuestion:** «Брейншторм идёт всю ночь. Не давать Mac засыпать до 09:00?»
1. **Да, запусти caffeinate (рекомендую)** — `caffeinate -is -t 35400`, остановлю при уборке; сон обрывает ответы агентов и блокирует связку ключей.
2. **Настрою сам** — я ничего не запускаю.
3. **Нет, пусть засыпает** — работа встанет до утра, дизайна к утру не будет.

*English: "Keep the Mac awake until 09:00?" — yes, run caffeinate (recommended) / I'll set it myself / no, let it sleep.*

## 5. On the notifications

**`wgka.last`:** I re-run `git -C $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive status --porcelain` myself, then:

```bash
git -C $R worktree add $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs -b chore/wg-keepalive-docs origin/main
```

- **Agent tool (Sonnet)** writes the `ccs-it` snapshot, the design and plan status ("implemented — PR #165, `<sha>`") and the stale docs, from `$S/evidence/T8/` only, in that worktree.
- I check every claim against the evidence, commit, open the PR and merge it with `gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch` (docs-only).

Cleanup, **foreground**:
```bash
herdr tab close <wgka tab_id>
git -C $R worktree remove $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
git -C $R worktree remove $R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs
git -C $R worktree prune && git -C $R pull
git -C $R branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay chore/wg-keepalive-docs
ps -p 48211 -o pid,command     # confirm it is my codex app-server
kill 48211
git -C $R worktree list
```

Then **Write** the verified lessons to memory with a `MEMORY.md` pointer, set T8 to `done` with `docs closed: yes`, and republish.

**`prod-*.last`:**
- I check `grep -F 'superpowers:'` on each transcript and each tab's context usage.
- Facts are answered with evidence; every choice goes as a neutral ballot to `adv-codex` and `adv-fable` at once.
- Round 2 and round 3 are relayed by file path.
- After both advisors confirm the joint doc, it goes to a 2/2 approval ballot, then `brainstormed`, and is published as a Russian Artifact.

## Why

- **T8 is not done at "accepted".** `done` needs the docs checklist and the cleanup, including the broker and my memory.
- **`wgka` is closed, not reused.** One tab is one task. RDP audio is a new task, so it starts at stage 0 with two product advisors, and no executor may exist before `brainstormed`. What `wgka` knows is in merged code and its closing report, which I verify.
- **I design nothing.** The brief carries the operator's words, facts with evidence, and one marked hypothesis.
- **"By morning" is a wish, not a waiver.** The full rounds can fit the night, so there is nothing to poll yet. If they cannot, slip-or-waive is the operator's call.
- **One poll.** Keeping the Mac awake changes the operator's environment, and they are about to leave.
- **Nine hours in,** my context is the scarce resource. Prose goes to a subagent, relays go by path, and state is on disk.
